Proposal, not applied. Optional per-side configure arguments for the perf lab runner.
Keys CONFIGURE_ARGS_A and CONFIGURE_ARGS_B replace the shared CONFIGURE_ARGS for one side.
A side that does not set its key keeps CONFIGURE_ARGS, so existing jobs, tree names and build stamps do not change.
With it, a future ./configure --lto can be tested as CONFIGURE_ARGS_B=--lto, without a source patch.
Tree name gets -c<hash of the arguments> when they differ from the shared ones, so A and B never build in one tree.
The build stamp (remote.sh, .lab-build) now hashes the arguments of that side.
perf-job.sh: one phase only when revs, patches and arguments are all equal.
Apply from the harness root with: patch -p1 < docs/perf/lto-pgo-runner-configure-args-ab.diff
Not covered: the CONFIGURE_ARGS row of the key table in docs/perf/perf-lab.md needs two more keys.

